  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{12} \\\\  & =1+3+\\frac{20}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
